{
  "an8.49:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.49 ",
  "an8.49:0.2": "5. Sabbath ",
  "an8.49:0.3": "Winning in This Life (1st) ",
  "an8.49:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery. ",
  "an8.49:1.2": "Then Visākhā, Migāra’s mother, went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. ",
  "an8.49:1.3": "The Buddha said to her: ",
  "an8.49:2.1": "“Visākhā, a lady who has four qualities is practicing to win in this life, and she succeeds at it. ",
  "an8.49:2.2": "What four? ",
  "an8.49:2.3": "It’s when a lady is well-organized at work, manages the domestic help, acts lovingly toward her husband, and preserves his earnings. ",
  "an8.49:3.1": "And how is a lady well-organized at work? ",
  "an8.49:3.2": "It’s when she’s deft and tireless in doing domestic duties for her husband, such as knitting and sewing. She understands how to go about things in order to complete and organize the work. ",
  "an8.49:3.3": "That’s how a lady is well-organized at work. ",
  "an8.49:4.1": "And how does a lady manage the domestic help? ",
  "an8.49:4.2": "It’s when she knows what work her husband’s domestic bondservants, servants, and workers have completed, and what they’ve left incomplete. ",
  "an8.49:4.3": "She knows who is sick, and who is fit or unwell. She distributes to each a fair portion of fresh and cooked foods. ",
  "an8.49:4.4": "That’s how a lady manages the domestic help. ",
